.TH "zoril" "1" "2026\-11\-03"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
zoril \- Self\-hosted compiler for the Zoril systems programming language
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBzoril\fR [\fIoptions\fR] <input.\&zrl>
.br
\fBzoril fmt\fR [\fB\-\-check\fR] <file.\&zrl>.\&.\&.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBzoril\fR is the self\-hosted frontend compiler for the Zoril systems programming language.\& It parses source files, checks type and memory safety rules, performs semantic analysis, and emits textual Zoril Intermediate Language (ZIL) or module interface files (.\&zri).\&
.PP
Zoril checks memory and type safety at compile time using region\-based arena allocations, affine ownership tracking, and non\-null fat pointers.\& For detailed information on the safety model and invariants, refer to \fBdoc/SAFETY.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
The compiler accepts exactly one input file.\& Specifying more than one input file, or an unrecognized option beginning with \fB\-\fR, is an error.\& The special argument \fB\-\-\fR terminates option processing, allowing file names that begin with a dash to be passed as the input.\&
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.PP
\fBzoril fmt\fR [\fB\-\-check\fR] <file.\&zrl>.\&.\&.\&
.RS 4
Format Zoril source files in place.\& If \fB\-\-check\fR is specified, \fBzoril fmt\fR does not modify files; instead, it lists unformatted files and exits with a non\-zero status if any formatting changes are needed.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display usage instructions and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display compiler version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-o\fR <file>
.RS 4
Write output to <file>.\& Defaults to \fBout.\&zil\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-I\fR <dir> | \fB\-I\fR <name>=<dir>
.RS 4
Add an include root.\& When specified as \fBname=dir\fR, the root anchors module identities under a logical package namespace.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-root\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Set the project root directory for module resolution.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-emit\-zil\fR
.RS 4
Emit textual ZIL (the default action).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-compile\-only\fR
.RS 4
Compile only the specified module without processing or linking dependencies (separate compilation).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-emit\-interface\fR
.RS 4
Write the module'\&s public interface summary (.\&zri) instead of ZIL.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-write\-interface\fR <file>
.RS 4
In addition to the primary output, write the module'\&s public interface to <file>.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-iface\-dir\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Read imported modules'\& cached interface definitions from <dir>.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-require\-interface\fR
.RS 4
Require an interface file under the interface directory for every import; treat missing interfaces as a fatal compilation error rather than falling back to parsing full module source.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-emit\-deps\fR
.RS 4
Print the dependency import graph reachable from the input module.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-emit\-zir\-stats\fR
.RS 4
Print a census of the ZIR constructs and CFG shape the input lowers to, one line per construct, and exit without emitting ZIL.\& Used by \fBscripts/check_route_coverage.\&sh\fR to check that the probes cited by a safety matrix row walk every route the row lists.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-emit\-origins\fR
.RS 4
Developer option.\& Print the origin sets of every function the input file defines \- for each local, the origins of the addresses it holds (O) and of the storage it owns (S), as described in \fBdoc/design/provenance.\&md\fR \- and exit without emitting ZIL; the exit status is the compile'\&s verdict.\& No rule reads the sets yet.\& Used by \fBscripts/test_origins.\&sh\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Report compilation progress, printing each phase, source file, and function as it is processed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-W\fR <lint> | \fB\-A\fR <lint>
.RS 4
Enable (\fB\-W\fR, warn) or disable (\fB\-A\fR, allow) the specified compiler lint.\& Supported lints include:
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBwildcard\-arm\fR: Warn when pattern matches contain catch\-all wildcard arms.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBredundant\-cast\fR: Warn on redundant type casts (disabled by default).\&
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-hosted\fR
.RS 4
Name the program'\&s entry \fBzoril_main\fR instead of \fBmain\fR, for a program linked into a libc process: \fBrt/runtime_hosted.\&o\fR defines the \fBmain\fR that C'\&s startup code calls and tail\-calls it.\& Link with \fBcc\fR, not \fBld\fR.\& Nothing else in the output changes, and a build without the flag is unchanged.\& A trap is libc'\&s \fBabort\fR (status 134) and does not flush C stdio.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-checked\fR
.RS 4
Developer option, not a user\-facing mode.\& Instrument the emitted program for memory\-safety testing: released arena space stays poisoned and is never handed out again, a local'\&s slot is poisoned where its scope ends, a dropped value is poisoned and a second drop of it traps (exit 134), and a heap block released twice traps instead of unmapping whatever lives there now.\& A release build contains none of it \- the instrumentation is emitted only under this flag, so the emitted ZIL of a program does not change \- and it is not a safety mode: nothing about what the compiler accepts changes.\& See \fBmake test\-checked\fR in \fBdoc/developer_guide.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-\fR
.RS 4
Terminate option processing.\& All subsequent arguments are treated as input file paths, even if they begin with a dash \fB\-\fR.\&
.PP
.PP
.RE
.SH SEPARATE COMPILATION AND INTERFACES
.PP
Zoril supports separate compilation using lightweight interface files (\fB.\&zri\fR).\& When compiling a module with \fB\-c\fR, the compiler generates a \fB.\&zil\fR object and, optionally with \fB\-\-write\-interface\fR, a \fB.\&zri\fR interface describing the public types, traits, functions, and memory summaries.\& Subsequent compilations can load the pre\-computed interface using \fB\-\-iface\-dir\fR, eliminating the need to re\-parse and re\-analyze upstream source dependencies.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Compilation, formatting, or query succeeded.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
A compilation, type checking, syntax, or command\-line argument error occurred.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB134\fR
.RS 4
A compiler internal assertion or memory constraint was violated (traps).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compile a standalone program manually using the five\-stage pipeline:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
cat << \&'EOF\&' > hello\&.zrl
import "io\&.zrl";
use io::println;

fn main() \-> i32 {
    println("Hello, World!");
    return 0;
}
EOF

zoril \-I /usr/local/share/zoril/stdlib \-\-emit\-zil \-o hello\&.zil hello\&.zrl
zilc hello\&.zil hello\&.ssa
qbe \-o hello\&.s hello\&.ssa
as \-o hello\&.o hello\&.s
ld \-o hello /usr/local/lib/zoril/runtime\&.o hello\&.o
\&./hello
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile a library module separately and produce its public interface:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
cat << \&'EOF\&' > math\&.zrl
pub fn add(a: i64, b: i64) \-> i64 {
    return a + b;
}
EOF

zoril \-I /usr/local/share/zoril/stdlib \-c \-o math\&.zil \-\-write\-interface math\&.zri math\&.zrl
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBzilc\fR(1), \fBzbuild\fR(1), \fBzoril\-stdlib\fR(7)
